      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "A general practitioner's (GP's) daily workload includes an ever-increasing number of patients who are overweight and obese. A number of Australian guidelines are aimed at assisting GPs who are managing this group of adult patients."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "The objective of this article is to synthesise selected national Australian guidelines for GPs in the management of adults who are overweight or obese."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "Relevant national guidelines were chosen and reviewed by three GPs. The recommendations were amalgamated and any discrepancies were discussed within the research team."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "We presented a synthesis of the guidelines under headings that will assist GPs in a structured approach to managing patients who are overweight and obese."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "DISCUSSION",
          "content": "This synthesis forms the basis for developing a practical toolkit to assist GPs in managing adult patients who are overweight and obese."
        }
      ]},
